{"additions":795,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nPart of #148, closes #152.\n\n- A **Roadmap-layout saved view** renders a timeline: item rows on the left (icon, number, title), a time scale on the right with one bar per item, a yellow **today marker**, month labels, week ticks and shaded **iteration bands**.\n- **Spans** resolve locally (`domain/roadmap.rs`, no date crate — civil-days math): date fields by name (`start` / `begin` → start, `target` / `end` / `due` / `finish` → end; a single date field is a point, a missing end mirrors the start), falling back to the iteration field's `startDate` + `duration`. Items without a span are listed without a bar (with a hint line when nothing has one).\n- **Interaction** — `+` / `-` zoom month (1 cell = 3 days) / week (1 = 1) / day (3 = 1); `h` / `l` scroll the timeline; `j` / `k` move rows (the detail follows); `t` drops into the table and back to the view's own layout; draft bars render in a visible grey (dark grey sank into the selection background).\n- The date/zoom math, span/iteration resolution and pane behaviour are unit-tested; a `TestBackend` render test pins the selected row keeping its bar.\n\n## Docs / demo\n\n- Guide (en/ja) saved-views section + key tables (`+` / `-`), Config Reference action rows, README en/ja.\n- Demo project got `Start date` / `Target date` values (staggered spans + two point spans); `tape/demo-projects.tape` adds the Timeline view with zoom out/in; GIF re-recorded live — it also happens to show #164's `⚠ api N left` warning in action.\n\n## Tests\n\n373 green, clippy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w","changedFiles":12,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-07T08:07:33Z","deletions":16,"headRefName":"feat/projects-view-roadmap","labels":[],"number":165,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMb6BgA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nIt introduces a small but concrete correctness issue in date parsing (accepting impossible dates) and a misleading today-marker header comment/style mismatch that should be fixed before approval.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR implements the Projects page **Roadmap** saved-view layout by adding local date/span resolution and a new timeline renderer inside the existing projects board pane, along with updated keybindings, docs, and demo tape/GIF.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add `projects::domain::roadmap` for civil-day date math, span resolution (date fields + iteration fallback), and zoom scaling.\n- Extend `BoardPane` to support a new `BoardMode::Roadmap` with timeline rendering, zoom (`+`/`-`), and horizontal scroll (`h`/`l` / arrow keys).\n- Update docs/config reference and the projects demo tape/GIF to reflect the new Roadmap behavior and keybindings.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tape/demo-projects.tape | Demonstrates cycling into the Timeline/Roadmap view, zooming, and row navigation. |\r\n| src/projects/panes/board.rs | Adds `Roadmap` mode, zoom/scroll actions, and a timeline renderer with today marker and iteration bands. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/roadmap.rs | Introduces date parsing/civil-day math, span/iteration resolution, and zoom cell mapping with unit tests. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/mod.rs | Exposes the new `roadmap` domain module. |\r\n| README.md | Documents `+`/`-` roadmap zoom in the Projects key table. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese README update for roadmap zoom keys. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/views-projects.md | Documents the Roadmap view behavior and interaction model. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/config-reference.md | Adds `ZoomIn`/`ZoomOut` actions to the Projects config reference. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/views-projects.md | Japanese guide update for Roadmap view description and keys. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/config-reference.md | Japanese config reference update for roadmap zoom actions. |\r\n| assets/demo-projects.gif | Re-recorded demo GIF (LFS pointer updated). |\r\n| assets/default.kdl | Adds `+`/`-` bindings for `ZoomIn`/`ZoomOut` on the Projects page. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 12/12 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T08:10:29Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"59976edaa07fe09e107c5d55a6f8d652a48571d9"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMb8utg","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nThe Roadmap rendering has confirmed performance pitfalls and inconsistent horizontal scroll behavior across zoom levels that should be addressed before approval.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (3)\n\n**Previously missed (2)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**src/projects/panes/board.rs:683**\n* In Roadmap mode, horizontal scrolling uses a fixed 7-cell step regardless of zoom. Since `Zoom::Day` is 3 cells/day and `Zoom::Month` is 3 days/cell, this makes the scroll distance inconsistent (e.g., Day scroll is ~2.3 days, not ~1 week). Consider scaling the step by `self.zoom` so h/l (←/→) moves roughly the same number of days across zoom levels.\n**src/projects/panes/board.rs:1256**\n* Rendering iteration bands currently loops over the full band cell range (`bs..=be`) even when most of it is off-screen. For long-running projects/spans this can turn each render into a large O(span) loop; clamping to the visible cell range keeps the work bounded by terminal width.\n\nThis issue also appears on line 1379 of the same file.\n\n**src/projects/panes/board.rs:1383**\n* Roadmap bar rendering loops over every cell in the item's span (`zoom.x(start)..=zoom.x_end(end)`) and relies on `visible()` to filter. If an item spans months/years, this becomes unnecessarily expensive per row; clamp the loop to the visible cell range so each row render is O(chart_w).\n```\n                for x in zoom.x(*s0, origin)..=zoom.x_end(*e0, origin) {\n                    if let Some(c) = visible(x) {\n                        cells[c] = ('█', bar);\n                    }\n                }\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 12/12 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T08:15:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"ffc8dea84bcc799645e4cdaf5cb4438cd3634952"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMcNUeA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T08:45:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"ffc8dea84bcc799645e4cdaf5cb4438cd3634952"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMcNWDg","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-07T08:45:25Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"ffc8dea84bcc799645e4cdaf5cb4438cd3634952"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","complet